/*
========================================================================
 REVISION NOTES: DTO (Data Transfer Object) - Kyun Zaroori Hai
========================================================================

 Q: private field hai, getter/setter bhi hai - to DTO ki zarurat kya hai?

 ANSWER (Core Concept):
 -----------------------
 "private" sirf ye control karta hai -> JAVA CODE ke andar direct
 access na ho (user.password likh ke access nahi kar sakte).

 Lekin JSON response banane wala tool (Jackson, jo Spring internally
 use karta hai) "private" ko dekhta hi nahi. Wo sirf dekhta hai:
 "is class mein get___() naam ka PUBLIC method hai kya?"
 Agar hai, to Jackson use CALL karke JSON mein daal deta hai.

 Matlab: private field + public getter = field JSON mein LEAK ho jaati hai.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 PROOF (Bina DTO ke kya hota hai):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    public class User {
        private Long id;
        private String username;
        private String password;   // private hai
        private String role;

        public String getPassword() { return password; }  // PUBLIC getter
    }

    // Controller me agar ye kiya:
    return user;   // seedha Entity return kar diya

    // To Postman/Frontend ko ye JSON milega:
    {
      "id": 1,
      "username": "ankit123",
      "password": "$2a$10$hashedSecretPassword",   <-- LEAK HO GAYA!
      "role": "MEMBER"
    }

    WAJAH: Jackson ne getPassword() ko call kiya kyunki wo PUBLIC tha.
    "private" sirf Java-level protection hai, JSON-level nahi.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 DTO KYA SOLVE KARTA HAI (2 Problems):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

 1) SENSITIVE DATA LEAK
    - DTO me sirf wahi fields banao jo bhejni hain.
    - Field exist hi nahi karti -> Jackson ko getter milega hi nahi
      -> leak physically possible nahi.

 2) INFINITE LOOP / CRASH (Bidirectional Relationships)
    - Entity: User -> Member -> List<IssueRecord> -> wapas Member
      (bidirectional @OneToOne / @OneToMany relationship)
    - Seedha Entity return karne se Jackson circular reference me
      fasa kar StackOverflowError de sakta hai.
    - DTO me relationship ka poora nested object nahi hota,
      sirf zaroori flat data hota hai -> loop hi nahi banta.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 GOLDEN RULE (Yaad Rakhne Wali Line):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    ENTITY  = Database ka structure   (DB me kya STORE hoga)
    DTO     = API ka structure        (Client ko kya DIKHEGA)

    "private" batata hai -> kaun ANDAR SE access kar sakta hai
    DTO      batata hai -> kya BAHAR bhejna hai


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 JS/MERN ANALOGY (Apna Background Use Karke Yaad Rakh):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    // BINA DTO pattern ke (bura tareeka) - Express me:
    res.json(user);              // password bhi chala jaayega!

    // DTO jaisa pattern (accha tareeka) - Express me:
    res.json({
      username: user.username,
      role: user.role            // password jaan-bujh kar chhoda
    });

    Java me DTO isi manual-filtering ko FORMAL / REUSABLE class
    bana deta hai, taaki har controller me baar-baar naya object
    manually na banana pade.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 REQUEST vs RESPONSE DTO (Direction Samajh):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    Client --[RegisterRequest DTO]--> Controller --> Service --> Entity --> DB
    DB --> Entity --> Service --[LoginResponse DTO]--> Controller --> Client

    RegisterRequest : Client sirf username/password/email bhejta hai
                       (DB ka id, internal fields nahi bhejta)

    LoginResponse   : Server sirf token/username/role bhejta hai
                       (password kabhi bhi response me nahi jaata)


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 INTERVIEW ONE-LINER (Bolne Ke Liye Ready):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    "Entity database ka representation hai, DTO API contract hai.
     DTO use karte hain taaki sensitive fields expose na ho aur
     bidirectional JPA relationships serialize karte time infinite
     loop / StackOverflowError na aaye."

========================================================================
